                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e20ed6b-17a6-3eaf-a12d-460706fc1925",
                        "entry_id": "17a24346-6401-3bbc-9466-d238684de9eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Manie de l'écriture."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39aced11-58b7-4fa5-9f06-8011a5349dbf",
                                "sense_id": "4e20ed6b-17a6-3eaf-a12d-460706fc1925",
                                "text": "Le lobe temporal de l’épilepsie est associé à l’hypergraphie. Ce lien a été effectué en 1974 (Waxman SG, Geschwind N. Hypergraphia in temporal lobe epilepsy. Neurology. 1974;24:629-36). Nombre d’écrivains à l’oeuvre abondante y ont été sujets tels que Dostoïevski, Byron, Dante, Molière, Pétrarque, Poe, Tennyson…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e88b59bf-9919-32fa-8415-74982cd92f26",
                        "entry_id": "17a24346-6401-3bbc-9466-d238684de9eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lettrisme, courant esthétique inventé par Isidore Isou en 1950, aussi nommé « métagraphie »."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb52ca2f-78d4-458b-9504-aafb67858920",
                                "sense_id": "e88b59bf-9919-32fa-8415-74982cd92f26",
                                "text": "L'hypergraphie peut se définir comme un art basé sur l'organisation de l'ensemble des signes concrets de la communication visuelle (alphabétiques, lexiques, ou idéographiques) acquis ou possibles, existants ou inventés. (Wikipedia, « Lettrisme »)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3537f740-e5c0-40f1-bede-f796b21fa38a",
                        "source_entry_id": "17a24346-6401-3bbc-9466-d238684de9eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypergraphia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypergraphia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d107a4f2-ca4d-354d-9f74-d16bb0ec1752",
                                        "entry_id": "79a28753-163c-3e6a-a9ad-95a55ebbafc4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A behavioural condition characterised by an intense desire to write, associated with changes in the temporal lobes due to epilepsy or chemical changes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b10b187-cf28-4307-9541-916205ec9ad3",
                                                "sense_id": "d107a4f2-ca4d-354d-9f74-d16bb0ec1752",
                                                "text": "Two features of the interictal behavior syndrome are relevant: hypergraphia or the tendency to write compulsively and often repetitively, and verbosity or loquaciousness, the tendency to be overly talkative, rambling, and circumstantial in speech."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65c463ff-5ed5-4dde-ab88-1bd1c348ddb2",
                                                "sense_id": "d107a4f2-ca4d-354d-9f74-d16bb0ec1752",
                                                "text": "There is some suggestion that hypergraphia is associated with non-dominant hemisphere temporal lobe disturbances (Trimble, 1986c)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c6cdef0-7bc4-424e-853f-be4b95b58e71",
                                                "sense_id": "d107a4f2-ca4d-354d-9f74-d16bb0ec1752",
                                                "text": "Two cases of mania and hypergraphia in patients with temporal lobe epilepsy were reported by Sanders and Mathews (1994). In the first case, a 58-year-old right-handed man suffered a ruptured right middle cerebral artery aneurism, which required a craniotomy. During interictal periods, the patient demonstrated hypergraphia, as well as several episodes of alternating manic and mildly depressive phases."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1e43068-11fa-4db1-923e-c2cfa7c87682",
                        "source_entry_id": "17a24346-6401-3bbc-9466-d238684de9eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "graphomania",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "graphomania",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "137f6831-d3fc-31b5-a4ca-738c55f09ef4",
                                        "entry_id": "1ba5d438-30af-308c-b416-53d82f813aff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The compulsion to write."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cf38d71-d62d-4ea6-a203-1a3785e974ab",
                                                "sense_id": "137f6831-d3fc-31b5-a4ca-738c55f09ef4",
                                                "text": "Wagner’s graphomania is shown not only by the substance, but also by the outward form of his writings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99568c54-03c3-3b32-9e36-0ec90f6f0884",
                                        "entry_id": "1ba5d438-30af-308c-b416-53d82f813aff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used as part of the name of various surrealist techniques, e.g., a method in which dots are made at the sites of impurities in a blank sheet of paper, and lines are then made between the dots; see \\\"Entoptic graphomania\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36aac8ed-805b-40bc-8335-50e8b718975a",
                                                "sense_id": "99568c54-03c3-3b32-9e36-0ec90f6f0884",
                                                "text": "A devoted explorer of decalcomania, fumage, frottage, collage and other methods of pictorial automatism, Colquhoun invented several magic-inspired techniques of her own, including graphomania, stillomania, and parsemage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
